        {
          "tag": "h1",
          "attrs": {},
          "html": "Caresse vs Bonded :<br><em>before, or during?</em>"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "hero-sub"
          },
          "html": "Bonded is there to plan a scene in writing. But you have to reply at each step for it to move on, which makes it impractical in the heat of the moment. Caresse covers both: the planning, then a session that plays on its own, using your first names, without ever touching the screen."
